}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-311_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"05f74084-8156-4489-b43f-fbb9222cdc20","comments":[],"created_at":1795271730961173001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9334a92e-1eb5-4a28-bbe0-e27a9644d3c8","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"98a7-07c4-fc4d-4e08"}],"description":"## Goal\n\nLand a regression test proving bug reponsible-exposed-okapi's premise false: a reconciler pass that fails mid-apply (a reclaim fetched mid-pass refusing an inbound write, or any exception) loses no inbound import and duplicates no Jira mutation, once the failed pass's uncommitted state is discarded as the production bridge does.\n\n## Approach\n\nTest-only; no production code changes. One new module, `tests/integration/reconciler/test_inbound_import_replayed_after_failed_pass.py`, drives real passes over the stateful fake Jira from `test_reconcile_idempotency.py` (fixtures imported, not copied) with a committed 20-binding tracker. A pass's inbound EDIT write raises after a new issue DIG-2's inbound create wrote its Jira identity markers; then the uncommitted tracker state is discarded, as a fresh checkout would.\n\nMechanism it pins: `applier.apply` applies inbound before outbound, so the failed pass makes no outbound Jira write. The binding walk's level-triggered ADOPT arm (`binding_walk._adopt_stands_down`: a lone marker equal to the deterministic inbound id, with no binding and no local ticket) replays the import on the next pass, gated by the blast-radius breaker (`max_acting_fraction`, default 0.10). Production holds 5953 confirmed bindings, so a failed pass would need more than 595 orphaned imports before the breaker holds them.\n\n## Scope\n\nIn: the new test module only. Out: any reconciler change.\n\n## Testing\n\nThe module itself: (1) for a reclaim refusal and for a RuntimeError, the failed pass's only Jira writes are DIG-2's 2 identity markers; the next pass imports and binds DIG-2 with one CREATE, applies DIG-101's Jira rename, makes no `create_issue`, keeps one `rebar-id:` label; a further pass makes no Jira write and no new event. (2) With 1 confirmed binding the replay is held and `binding_walk_breaker_refused` is logged with an EXCEEDS reason. (3) A marker naming another local id is not adopted. (4) A surviving local import that lost its binding row is not imported a second time. All pass on current main; `make verify` passes.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A regression test shows that after a pass fails with a mid-pass reclaim refusal (and with a RuntimeError) and its uncommitted state is discarded, the next pass imports and binds the orphaned Jira issue with exactly one CREATE event, no `create_issue` call and a single identity label, and a further pass makes no Jira write.\n- [ ] A test shows the failed pass made no Jira write other than the inbound create's 2 identity markers.\n- [ ] Tests show the breaker holds an over-cap replay and logs `binding_walk_breaker_refused`, a marker naming another local id is not adopted, and a surviving local import is not imported twice.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/integration/reconciler/test_inbound_import_replayed_after_failed_pass.py","reason":"proof that a failed pass loses no inbound import"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"2b4983be-1b32-44ca-a045-f5093cc24fab","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"358c-cddf-92e7-48b0","ticket_type":"task","title":"Prove a failed bridge pass loses no inbound import","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["70b489da-c772-4946-9d4a-f68c28c3d214","9334a92e-1eb5-4a28-bbe0-e27